WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.400 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the mountains of northern Yemen, little
Shlomo grew up beside his father, Zechariah.

2
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.800 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
His father died when Shlomo was about three.

3
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:19.950 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The study house, a few years later.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.570 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“There were four of us children to one book.”

5
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.160 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“And this way we could read the book…”

6
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:31.720 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the front or the back, from the right or
the left.

7
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.600 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We could read it.”

8
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.415 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“When my mother died, I was perhaps fifteen.”

9
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.850 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After losing his parents, he went to live with
his aunt Badra.

10
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.760 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Work, too, was part of Shlomo’s childhood.

11
00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.070 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We worked as blacksmiths.”

12
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.350 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the workshop they shaped iron and learned to
guide each hammer blow.

13
00:00:50.545 --> 00:00:53.785 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
At nineteen, as he remembered it, he left the
mountains.

14
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:59.780 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo set off on foot, leaving the stone
houses of the mountains behind.

15
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.580 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“On donkeys.”

16
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.290 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“It took us about two weeks.”

17
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.830 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From place to place. We walked by day and
slept at night.”

18
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.700 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Mountain paths gave way to valleys. The journey
went on, day after day.

19
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.600 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Each evening they stopped to sleep. The next
day, they set out again.

20
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.850 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the mountains around Saada, the caravan
headed south.

21
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.780 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Roughly 600–700 km. He recalled about two weeks
on foot and with donkeys.

22
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.300 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Aden, the boy who had shared a book now had
pupils of his own.

23
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.970 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“I had children there, and I taught them.”

24
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.230 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“How old are you? I told them twenty-five.”

25
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.990 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
He remembered being twenty at the time.

26
00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.440 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“In the end they approved my aliyah.”

27
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:55.930 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After about a year of teaching and waiting, it
was time to sail.

28
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.290 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From Aden we went by ship.”

29
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.750 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Until now the journey was measured in
footsteps. From here the sea would carry him.

30
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:13.150 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The ship sailed north through the Red Sea to
the Suez Canal.

31
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.390 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We stayed in Port Said for one day.”

32
00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:27.250 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From there they sent us a car from the Land of
Israel.”

33
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.730 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Beyond the canal, the road carried them east,
all the way to Tel Aviv.

34
00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.410 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Tel Aviv, Shlomo found a bed at the
immigrants’ hostel.

35
00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.640 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In 1938, Yona Nakash and Shlomo Keha married.

36
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.360 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Yona was 17–18 and Shlomo was 30–31.

37
00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:54.020 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Four years later, in 1942, Yona and Shlomo
posed with their family.

38
00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:59.400 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo is 35 and Yona is 20–21.

39
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:05.060 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Ruti is 2–3 and Elisheva is under one year old.
